implementationPlan.description:
Adversarial self-review (load adversarial-self-review) of the two-file diff. Check:
- an off-by-one at the cap: MAX parses and MAX+1 is refused;
- a reader that still loads the whole file, such as File.length() followed by readText, or readBytes without a bound;
- the stream is closed on every path (use);
- no file deletion or new write for the oversize case;
- the log message never echoes file content;
- concurrent connect retries read the file independently, with no shared state;
- a daemon.json that vanishes between exists() and open is caught as an IOException and yields null;
- no behaviour change for valid files or under either profile.
Out of scope, noted only: the daemon (packages/moe-daemon/src/index.ts readDaemonInfo), moe-proxy (readDaemonInfoResult) and the wrapper pre-flight also read daemon.json without a cap. A FIFO at that path could block open(); git cannot commit FIFOs, so that is a residual. If the review changes bytes, re-run the step 3 gate fresh. Report both paths in complete_step.modifiedFiles.
